@startuml
title A / M-A.03b - Recover existing effects and isolate notification\nUC-04 extensions 5a, 6a/6b/6c/6d, 7a and 9a
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #27465B
skinparam ArrowColor #27465B
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D9
hide footbox
autonumber
control "Operations Service" as Ops
control "Domain Service" as Domain
database "Case / work / audit store" as Store
participant "Simulated return/label port" as Provider
participant "Simulated notification port" as Notify

Ops -> Domain : Reload persisted command and attempt history
Domain -> Store : Read durable identities, effects and work claims
Store --> Domain : Saved facts; never reset by a retry request
Domain --> Ops : Current snapshot
alt Prior command SUCCEEDED
  Ops -> Domain : Reuse saved result; do not invoke provider
else Prior EXECUTING / RECONCILING with another live worker
  break Another worker still holds the invocation / lookup claim
    note over Ops, Domain : Yield without changing the winner's attempt.
  end
else UNKNOWN, or orphaned EXECUTING / RECONCILING
  Ops -> Domain : Request authorised recovery claim
  Domain -> Store : Validate orphan recovery; reclaim lookup work atomically;\nrecord UNKNOWN then RECONCILING when writable (MA-D02)
  break No recovery authority, claim or storage
    note over Ops, Store : Retain uncertainty; no dispatch and no invented saved status.
  end
  Ops -> Provider : Query original provider_operation_id / fingerprint
  Provider --> Ops : Confirmed success / confirmed no effect / inconclusive
  Ops -> Domain : Submit typed reconciliation observation
  alt Confirmed successful effect
    Domain -> Store : Save original result + SUCCEEDED + audit
  else Proven no effect
    Domain -> Store : Save FAILED + absence evidence + audit
    note over Ops, Domain : A later internal retry requires G-RETRY and G-DISPATCH.\nMA-D01 proposes a new operation_id, preserving old records\nand the same logical command/key/fingerprint under the same approval.\nThe reconcile endpoint itself never means "execute again".
  else Unknown or lookup unavailable
    Domain -> Store : Save UNKNOWN + reason (MA-D02)
    opt Recovery budget exhausted and no accepted rejection/manual outcome
      Domain -> Store : Escalate case; preserve unresolved operation
    end
    note over Domain, Store : An accepted rejection/manual outcome keeps its case and\nnotification state, even if this historical lookup stays unknown.
  end
else Prior FAILED / BLOCKED
  note over Ops, Domain : No unconditional repeat. FAILED needs proven retry safety.\nExpired/changed approval or scope needs explicit new authority;\ncross-approval provider-key mapping remains MA-Q02.
end

group Accepted outcome takes priority over historical effect results
  Domain -> Store : Read current accepted outcome, notification and saved effects
  alt Accepted outcome is REJECTED or MANUAL_HANDLED
    Domain -> Store : Retain that outcome and its existing notification work
    note over Domain, Store : Historical success updates attempt facts and audit only.\nNever replace this outcome or queue RETURN_CREATED work.
  else Execution remains eligible and both effects succeeded without contradictory uncertainty
    Domain -> Store : Atomically recheck case/outcome version;\npersist or reuse RETURN_CREATED work and NOTIFICATION_PENDING
  else No deliverable outcome
    break Return/label unfinished, unresolved or current state ineligible
      note over Ops, Domain : Preserve all effects; no completion or new notification.\nA later eligible label needs current G-DISPATCH.
    end
  end
  group Deliver only the current persisted outcome
    break Notification SENT already saved
      note over Ops, Store : Return saved terminal outcome; no new notification.
    end
    Domain -> Store : Recheck current outcome/work identity atomically;\nclaim its unsent notification once, without replacing the outcome
    break Outcome changed, work not committed or claim not held
      note over Ops, Store : No send; retain saved outcome and recover existing work later.
    end
    Domain --> Ops : Committed notification-only work reference
    Ops -> Notify : Send saved outcome under notification idempotency key
    Notify --> Ops : Confirmed delivery or uncertain/failed delivery
    Ops -> Domain : record_notification_result(id, observation)
    break Observation does not match the current outcome/work binding
      note over Domain, Store : Reject stale observation; preserve current state and outcome.\nRecord safe denial evidence without changing notification status.
    end
    alt Delivery success matches current notification and accepted outcome
      Domain -> Store : Save SENT + audit; choose terminal from saved outcome
      alt Outcome is RETURN_CREATED and both valid results remain saved
        Domain -> Store : Case COMPLETED
      else Outcome is REJECTED
        Domain -> Store : Case REJECTED
      else Outcome is MANUAL_HANDLED
        Domain -> Store : Case MANUAL_HANDLED
      end
    else Delivery failed or remains uncertain
      Domain -> Store : Save pending / failed notification and recovery context
      note over Ops, Notify : Any retry repeats this saved notification only.\nNo return/label replay; historical attempt facts stay intact.
    end
    note over Domain, Store : If any local write fails, retain the last durable state;\nrecover the existing notification work without replaying operations.
  end
end
legend bottom
  MA-0.2 candidate walkthrough, not a performed provider test.
  Expired approval may allow authorised historical lookup, never a new effect.
  A historical lookup never changes an accepted rejection/manual outcome.
endlegend
@enduml
